{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400857-accuracy-without-distance-not-an-sos-question","id":1400857,"title":"Accuracy Without Distance (Not an SOS question!)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-03T17:21:46-07:00","id":1400857,"title":"Accuracy Without Distance (Not an SOS question!)","content":"In this first post, I\u2019ll simply copy the text of Accuracy Without Distance, posing the question in the next post so that I can edit in the answer if we reach a consenses. The Charm tags aren\u2019t relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Solar extends her anima through her hands and into her weapons, joining archer, target and arrow into a single being. As long as she is making an Archery-based attack, this Charm allows the Solar to complete an aim action in- stantly, and converts the subsequent three bonus dice into automatic non-Charm successes. An Essence 5+ repur- chase allows the Solar to fire a withering version of this attack against a crashed opponent. This attack rolls damage even if the attack roll generated no successes. This effect may only be used on a target once per crash period. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:22:19-07:00","id":1400858,"title":"","content":"What is the scope of the final two clauses in Accuracy Without Distance?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Autohit, once per crash affect both? </div> </div> </div>Or<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Autohit, once per crash affect withering only? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  Posing question 07-03-2020, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:45:44-07:00","id":1400863,"title":"","content":"Withering only as the second sentence refers to the first sentence of the repurchase. This attack roll refers to the An essence 5+ repurchase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T18:08:43-07:00","id":1400868,"title":"","content":"I'd say the once per crash clause only effects withering, since the withering version states it can only be used in crash and the decisive doesn't.<br /> <br /> I think the ordering wouldn't make sense for that to be true and the auto-hit applies to decisive, so that's probably withering only","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T02:21:48-07:00","id":1400920,"title":"","content":"The withering effect (this effect) is once per Crash.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the tags on this Charm aren't relevant, but if the Charm had a tag like Uniform this would be unambiguous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:02:50-07:00","id":1400970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400857-accuracy-without-distance-not-an-sos-question?p=1400920#post1400920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The withering effect (this effect) is once per Crash.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the autohit feature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T11:29:11-07:00","id":1400974,"title":"","content":"I think the autohit is decisive only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T12:19:22-07:00","id":1400984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400857-accuracy-without-distance-not-an-sos-question?p=1400974#post1400974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the autohit is decisive only.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The auto hit comes with the repurchase that works on a withering attack against a crashed opponent. Why would it work on the decisive? And if it did, why only the decisive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T13:15:27-07:00","id":1400990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400857-accuracy-without-distance-not-an-sos-question?p=1400984#post1400984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The auto hit comes with the repurchase that works on a withering attack against a crashed opponent. Why would it work on the decisive? And if it did, why only the decisive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, upon another reading I think the autohit is only on the withering damage, although I'm not sure how you calculate it. I guess you're assumed to hit with no threshold successes, although in previous editions of Exalted it specified how many threshold successes you were assumed to hit by.<br /> <br /> I was thinking the auto hit was decisive exactly for that reason, since it doesn't matter about threshold at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T13:52:04-07:00","id":1400996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400857-accuracy-without-distance-not-an-sos-question?p=1400990#post1400990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, upon another reading I think the autohit is only on the withering damage, although I'm not sure how you calculate it. I guess you're assumed to hit with no threshold successes, although in previous editions of Exalted it specified how many threshold successes you were assumed to hit by.<br /> <br /> I was thinking the auto hit was decisive exactly for that reason, since it doesn't matter about threshold at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, Sidereals had a charm that did this I believe in their melee tree in 2e. At least I think they did but my 2e books are at a friends house. Basically you'd use raw damage vs soak and go from their as normal. It's actually not any different from the normal rules as attacker wins on a tie. So if your evasion were 5 and I scored 5 successes I'd win and do withering equal to my normal raw without any roll over from succeses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T16:34:50-07:00","id":1401218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400857-accuracy-without-distance-not-an-sos-question?p=1400990#post1400990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, upon another reading I think the autohit is only on the withering damage, although I'm not sure how you calculate it. I guess you're assumed to hit with no threshold successes, ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. You resolve raw damage normally for step two of a withering attack: Strength + Weapon + Threshold Successes, with the later clearly being zero when your attack roll generated no successes at all.<br /> <br /> It is still much better than not dealing withering damage at all when you missed a crashed opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T21:42:57-07:00","id":1401428,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I'm getting a 'clear as mud' vibe here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T23:27:25-07:00","id":1401438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1400857-accuracy-without-distance-not-an-sos-question?p=1400970#post1400970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the autohit feature?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is specific to the Withering effect. As it is, you know, specific to the Withering effect: &quot;This attack&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for damage, if you don't have any Threshold Successes then you can't add them to damage. Strength + Weapon damage.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> The Charm is Decisive Only. It can only be used on Decisive Attacks. You Aim instantly and convert the bonus dice to successes. This is one effect.<br /> <br /> An Essence 5 repurchase allows for a Withering Only effect. This must be used against a Crashed opponent. It also allows you to Aim instantly and convert the bonus dice to successes. Should your rolled successes not overcome Defense because you have 0 net successes on the Difficulty, roll damage anyway. As you don't have any Threshold Successes, you can't as them to your (Strength + Weapon damage).<br /> <br /> It's a poorly written Charm, mostly because of 3E's use of natural language over precise system terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}